# Frontend rules

- Next.js App Router + React functional components + strict TypeScript.
- Prefer Server Components by default; use Client Components only when browser interactivity/state requires them.
- Feature-oriented structure: feature-specific code under `features/`; shared primitives under `shared/`.
- MobX is for client/UI domain state, not authoritative server/financial/auth state.
- Server data must be refetched/revalidated from API/source of truth; do not invent optimistic financial balances.
- SCSS Modules for component styles; co-locate styles where practical.
- Use reusable design tokens/variables rather than scattered magic colors/sizes.
- Accessible forms: labels, focus, keyboard behavior, `aria-*` where needed, meaningful errors.
- Never expose provider/payment secrets or internal admin permissions in browser bundles.
- Never call ProxyAPI/payment providers directly from frontend.
- Never render AI/user HTML via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without a reviewed sanitizer. Prefer safe text/Markdown with raw HTML disabled.
- Do not use browser-native validation bubbles as the only validation UX. Render Vimla-controlled localized field/form errors.
- Do not hard-code end-user text. Follow the i18n rule.
- UI must handle loading, empty, partial, retryable error and terminal error states explicitly.
